
[Forth for ARM Cortex-M4: planning]

This project will be for implementation and testing a
direct-threaded Forth kernel for the ARM Cortex-M4,
which will run from ROM and allow further code (Forth words)
to be compiled into RAM.

It is proposed to develop a DTC (direct-threaded code) implementation,
(as described here, https://www.bradrodriguez.com/papers/moving1.htm)
using an existing 32-bit Forth and replacing all assembler code and directives
as necessary in its source code and files. 

For reference, Z382 Camel Forth is a 32-bit Forth based on the papers by Rodriguez.
Find the source code in ./tmp/32bit/CAML382/asm for the following files 
CAML382d.S: CPU and Model Dependencies
  - this would define the architecture
CAML382.S: Code Primitives
CAML382h.S: High Level Words

This will require ARM assembler.

Target MCU for validating the port will be the STM32G474,
which utilizes 32-bit Arm Cortex-M4 RISC core with floating point unit.

PlatformIO can be utilized for this. Refer to folder ../x-nucleo-ihm07m1

Research as necessary and place any retrieved documents (such as PDF) in ./doc/reference or ./doc/datasheets accordingly.

We need to agree on a strategy and arrive at an implementation plan with clear phases and milestones. 
